                <pb facs="1118" n="1016" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg1016"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/198a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-24T16:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Since matter of recognition of Spanish Zone by this Government and the
                    settlement of claims by Spain has been pending for approximately 6 months, the
                    Foreign Office having informed the Embassy in February it was pressing for an
                    answer from the Spanish High Commissioner at Tetuan, you are requested, within
                    your discretion, to ascertain orally, if possible, what the Spanish Government
                    proposes to do in the matter. It would appear that sufficient time has elapsed
                    for a decision upon the question. Please cable brief reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
